% A note on our itemize conventions:
% Use (I) if the items have an "And" relation (IA1)
% Use (1) if the items have an "Or" relation (1Ai)
% Use (i) if the items are different parts of a proposition (iA1)
% Use (A) if the items are different equivalent (or inequivalent) conditions (A1i)
% Use (a) if the items are equations (i.e. if you are in an align environment (a1i))
% Use 1. if the items are the steps of a procedure; in this case, i. should be used for sub-steps
% Otherwise, use bullet points (e.g. if you are writing out a list of definitions)


